      "notes": "The verdict is well-structured and evidence-grounded. The 'stated' tier claim E10 is technically from a secondary source summary rather than the policy text M, but it is corroborated by M and labelled 'stated' plausibly as policy-stated intent \u2014 a warning-level concern at most, and the content is consistent with M. The measurable claim about UKSPF being 'targeted at economically disadvantaged areas' slightly overstates E6 (which only gives the funding figure, not the targeting criterion), but E17 and the broader evidence set support this characterisation, so not blocking. The mixed direction is genuinely supported by claims on both sides: positive (UKSPF extension preserves skills/jobs funding) and negative (redirection to National Service harms deprived areas). Confidence is appropriately low. No party-blind or lever-leakage issues detected."
